+#### [OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF)
+> **Description:** `OCRmyPDF` adds a searchable OCR text layer to scanned PDFs while preserving the original document structure and producing scriptable output. Its README focuses on command-line automation, PDF/A output, page rotation, deskewing, and multi-language support through Tesseract. Accountants often need this exact capability before archival search, month-end review, or audit retrieval can happen. While it is not an end-to-end AI copilot, it is a practical building block in nearly every self-hosted finance document pipeline. GitHub shows 32.1k stars, Python as primary language, MPL-2.0 licensing, and an update on Dec 15, 2025.
