+## TL;DR
+- `PaddleOCR`, `MinerU`, `docTR`, and `invoice2data` are the strongest open-source starting points for invoice, receipt, and PDF extraction.
+- `NeuralForecast`, `Darts`, `Chronos`, and `Merlion` are the most useful forecasting and anomaly-detection repos for FP&A, cash flow planning, and close monitoring.
+- `Vanna`, `PandasAI`, `DB-GPT`, and `Dataherald` are the most relevant GitHub-native SQL copilots for finance analysts who live in spreadsheets, warehouses, and BI tools.
+- `Langflow`, `Flowise`, `Activepieces`, and `Haystack` are the best orchestration layers for building private accountant-facing copilots and document workflows.
+- Pure GitHub-first accountant-only AI repos are still rare, so the best stack today is usually a combination of OCR, text-to-SQL, forecasting, and automation building blocks.
