+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for accountants in 2026?
+If you need invoice and PDF extraction, start with `PaddleOCR`, `MinerU`, `docTR`, and `invoice2data`. If you need forecasting or anomaly detection, `NeuralForecast`, `Darts`, `Chronos`, and `PyOD` are the strongest picks. If you need natural-language access to finance databases, look first at `Vanna`, `PandasAI`, `DB-GPT`, and `Dataherald`.
+
+### Are there truly accountant-specific AI GitHub repos?
+Not many. That is the main gap this research surfaced. Most strong public GitHub repos are broader document AI, forecasting, SQL, or workflow tools that accountants can adapt, rather than turnkey "AI for accountants" products.
+
+### Which open source AI repos are best for invoice processing and accounts payable?
+`invoice2data` is the most AP-specific extractor in this list. `PaddleOCR`, `Surya`, `MinerU`, `docTR`, and `OCRmyPDF` are stronger when scans, tables, or multilingual layouts make invoices harder to normalize.
+
+### Which GitHub AI tools help accountants forecast cash flow or spot anomalies?
+For forecasting, start with `NeuralForecast`, `Darts`, `Chronos`, and `Orbit`. For exception monitoring and fraud-style outlier detection, `PyOD` and `Merlion` are the most directly useful.
+
+### What is the best self-hosted AI SQL copilot for accounting data?
+`Vanna` is the cleanest GitHub-native text-to-SQL option for many finance teams. `DB-GPT` is broader and more platform-like. `PandasAI` is often the easiest choice when finance users mostly work with CSVs, extracts, and DataFrames instead of a single warehouse.
+
+### Are these repositories safe to use with financial data?
+Safer than opaque SaaS by default, but not automatically safe. You still need to review licenses, deployment architecture, model providers, audit logging, retention rules, secrets handling, and whether the tool sends data to external APIs. In particular, mixed-license projects such as `Activepieces`, `Automatisch`, and `Open WebUI` deserve extra review.
